[00:01.32] (Jeannie Seely)
[00:13.15] You don't listen even when I beg you not to leave
[00:23.85] You don't hear what I'm saying 'cause you pay no attention to me
[00:37.61] And when you come home after being gone you have no alibi
[00:49.55] 'Cause you don't even care enough to lie.
[00:56.07] Would it take you very long to notice if I'm gone
[00:56.07] If sometimes I wasn't here when you came home
[00:56.07] You know I know where you go but you don't try to hide
[00:56.07] 'Cause you don't even care enough to lie.
